cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MomentBench: Corpus-Scale Video Moment Retrieval Benchmark"
message: "If you use MomentBench in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: Mixpeek
    website: https://mixpeek.com
repository-code: https://github.com/mixpeek/momentbench
url: https://momentbench.com
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2025-07-12"
keywords:
  - video retrieval
  - temporal grounding
  - benchmark
  - multimodal
  - moment localization
abstract: >-
  MomentBench is a corpus-scale video moment retrieval benchmark comprising
  75 hours of rights-cleared video across three verticals (civic proceedings,
  aerospace operations, archival film) with 500 human-annotated queries
  spanning four difficulty tiers. All footage is public domain or CC BY.
  The benchmark measures whether systems can locate an exact moment — the
  correct video and the correct sub-5-second window — across the full corpus.
